    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/skill/sub-kg-lifecycle",
      "@type": "bootstrap:Skill",
      "ambiguous": false,
      "description": "A sub-KG is a knowledge graph staged as a directory inside a harnessed repository, declared as its own layer, that may later leave for a repository of its own. The lifecycle: declare it in place, grow it, stage it for separation (one import seam, the separation guard, a self-contained rehearsal), and then, each behind an explicit owner confirmation, create the repository, copy the staged contents in with history, re-point the declaration, verify on a fresh clone and delete the in-repo copy. The light sibling of kg-separation: use this for a DATA layer that leaves whole, and kg-separation when a graph must split into a content repository and a tools repository.",
      "hasIOContract": false,
      "hasInstructions": true,
